{title: In the wilderness}
{subtitle: Isaiah 40:3}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Comfort falls like morning light
Your God speaks to the soul tonight
Speak tenderly to the city gate
Her hard service is paid and late
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Guilt is washed away in the rain
Double payment for the pain
A voice cries out through the night [Bb]
[Gm]Prepare the way in the [Dm]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In the wilderness prepare the [Bb]way
Make straight [Gm]in the desert a highway for our [Dm]God
Every valley lifted high
Mountains [Bb]made low to the sky [Gm][Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Rugged ground becomes a plain
Rough places smoothed by His name
The glory of the Lord is [Bb]seen
[Gm]All flesh together in the green [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In the wilderness prepare the [Bb]way
Make straight in [Gm]the desert a highway for our [Dm]God
Every valley lifted high
Mountains made [Bb]low to the sky [Gm][Dm]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
A voice says cry out loud [Bb]
[Gm]What shall I cry in this [Dm]crowd
All flesh is grass and flower
Fading [Gm]like dust on the power [Dm]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In the wilderness prepare the [Bb]way
Make straight in the [Gm]desert a highway for our [Dm]God
Every valley lifted high
Mountains made low [Bb]to the sky
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The mouth of the Lord has spoken
Com[Gm]fort is never bro[Dm]ken
{end_of_verse}
